<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Stage 45 – Full Candle Integration</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../styles.css" />
</head>

<body class="theme-dark">

<header class="top-bar">
  <a href="../lessons.html" class="icon-button">←</a>
  <h1 class="app-title">Stage 45 – Full Candle Integration</h1>
  <button id="theme-toggle" class="icon-button">🌓</button>
</header>

<main class="main-content">

<section class="card">
  <h2 class="section-title">Everything Comes Together</h2>
  <p>
    This is the final stage of the Candlestick Mastery chapter. You’ve learned:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Candle strength</li>
    <li>Candle weakness</li>
    <li>Momentum</li>
    <li>Reversals</li>
    <li>Continuation</li>
    <li>Exhaustion</li>
    <li>Location</li>
    <li>Timing</li>
    <li>Volume</li>
    <li>Levels</li>
    <li>Trend shifts</li>
    <li>Breakouts + fakeouts</li>
    <li>Pullbacks</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Now you combine them with trend, moving averages, and structure to build disciplined,
    consistent trade ideas.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="card">
  <h2 class="section-title">Candles Confirm — They Don’t Predict</h2>
  <p>
    You never trade a candle alone. You trade a candle inside a system:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Trend first</li>
    <li>Structure second</li>
    <li>Moving averages third</li>
    <li>Candles confirm the idea</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This is how you avoid emotional trading and stay disciplined.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- QUIZ -->
<section class="card">
  <h2 class="section-title">Final Candlestick Quiz</h2>
  <form id="lesson45-quiz" class="form">

    <label class="form-label">
      What comes first in this academy?
      <select name="q1" class="form-input" required>
        <option value="">Select</option>
        <option value="a">Trend + structure + MAs.</option>
        <option value="b">Candle patterns alone.</option>
        <option value="c">Impulse.</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <label class="form-label">
      What is the role of candles?
      <select name="q2" class="form-input" required>
        <option value="">Select</option>
        <option value="a">Confirmation.</option>
        <option value="b">Prediction.</option>
        <option value="c">Emotion.</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <label class="form-label">
      What matters most?
      <select name="q3" class="form-input" required>
        <option value="">Select</option>
        <option value="a">Discipline.</option>
        <option value="b">Guessing.</option>
        <option value="c">Chasing candles.</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <div id="lesson45-quiz-message" class="feedback-text"></div>

    <div class="button-row">
      <button type="submit" class="primary-button">Submit Final Quiz</button>
    </div>

  </form>
</section>

<!-- SIMULATION -->
<section class="card">
  <h2 class="section-title">Final Simulation: Full Candle Integration</h2>
  <p>
    Imagine an uptrend above rising moving averages. Price pulls back with small candles, forms
    an inside bar, then prints a bullish engulfing candle at the moving average.
  </p>

  <form id="lesson45-sim" class="form">

    <label class="form-label">
      What does this confirm?
      <select name="confirm" class="form-input" required>
        <option value="">Select</option>
        <option value="a">Buyers defended and regained control.</option>
        <option value="b">Sellers dominating.</option>
        <option value="c">Nothing meaningful.</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <label class="form-label">
      What is the disciplined response?
      <select name="discipline" class="form-input" required>
        <option value="">Select</option>
        <option value="a">Consider a call only if your full plan aligns.</option>
        <option value="b">Enter instantly.</option>
        <option value="c">Double size.</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <div id="lesson45-sim-message" class="feedback-text"></div>

    <div class="button-row">
      <button type="submit" class="primary-button">
        Complete Stage 45 — Candlestick Chapter Finished
      </button>
    </div>

  </form>
</section>

</main>

